I walk every morning.
But I also ride my bicycle sometimes.
Today my bicycle needs a service.
I take my bicycle to a shop.
I always come to this exact shop.
There is a mechanic in the shop.
I call him Dada.
I say, "Hello Dada."
Dada says, "Hello Madam."
Dada looks at my bicycle.
He says, "Okay Madam, I will do the servicing."
I ask, "Dada, when do I come for the bicycle?"
Dada says, "You come on Thursday."
I ask, "At what time on Thursday?"
Dada says, "Come at seven o'clock in the evening on Thursday."
My gym is at half past five on Thursday.
So I say, "Fine, I will come at seven o'clock."
I leave the bicycle right there.
And I walk back home.
